msgid "Splits an epoch into ordered sub-epochs (phases). Source is the parent epoch, target a phase (itself an EpochNode). Phases partition the parent's time-span; when hidden the parent epoch holds all the units, when shown the units are distributed across the phases. Reverse: is\\_in\\_epoch. 1.6.47 (MICRO-LAB orizzonti): the CHRONOLOGY reads it — the sub-epoch RESTRICTS the interval of its parent: its effective interval is the intersection of its own start/end with the parent's (a missing bound is the parent's; a bound outside the parent is brought back to it, with a warning), recursively. Graph.epoch\\_intervals() gives it, and a unit dated by its epoch reports rule «sub\\_epoch», source the parent epoch, relation has\\_sub\\_epoch when the bound came from the parent."
msgstr ""

